course: dictionary
lesson: 7655
title: One word, many meanings: prompt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word prompt has several meanings, so context decides which one you need. Look at the words around it. In «Her prompt reply made everyone smile», prompt is an adjective: she answered quickly, without delay. Try the swap test by putting in your meaning and checking that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Prompt can also be a verb. «The actor forgot her line, so the prompter whispered the next words.» A prompter fits with a play, so prompt here means to help someone remember words they forgot. Each meaning is a different job: be quick, cause an action, help someone remember, or give a signal that helps you start.
explain: Prompt is also a noun. «AI picture and music apps make a dragon or a song from a few typed words, called a prompt.» Here a prompt is the set of words you type to ask a computer for something. A writing prompt works the same way: it gives you an idea to start a story.
fact: Prompt as an adjective means done quickly, without delay, or on time: a prompt reply, or be prompt.
fact: Prompt as a verb can mean to cause someone to do something, or to help someone remember words they forgot.
fact: Prompt as a noun means words or a sign that help someone remember or start, such as a writing prompt.
fact: On a computer, a prompt is the message on the screen asking you to type something.
fact: «At six o'clock prompt» means exactly at six o'clock; this use is British.
exercise: «The train left at nine o'clock prompt.» What does prompt mean here? | Angry with the driver | Lost in the station | Very slowly | *Exactly on time
exercise: «The teacher gave us a writing prompt about a lost dog.» What is a writing prompt? | A long holiday from school | A type of pen for drawing | *Words or an idea that help you start a story | A punishment for being late
exercise: «The prompter whispered the next line to the actor.» What did the prompter do? | Painted the stage | Sang the song for the actor | *Helped the actor remember forgotten words | Closed the curtain
test: «Her prompt reply made everyone smile.» What does prompt mean? | Slow and careful | Rude and loud | *Quick, without delay | Hidden away
test: «The app asked her to type a prompt.» What is a prompt here? | A sound from a speaker | *Words typed in to ask a computer for something | A kind of tent | A picture hung on the wall
exam: Ananya says, «Prompt can mean on time, and it can mean to make something happen.» Which statement is correct? | Prompt is a type of animal | *Prompt has several meanings, so the context shows which one you need | Prompt means exactly the same as prompter in every sentence | Prompt only ever means slow
